1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,405
Next up: custom types with the Default Pattern. This problem is worth

2
00:00:04,505 --> 00:00:07,800
40 to 48 points, and the catch is that you can't use

3
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:13,220
class, extends, or super. You build everything from plain functions and prototypes.

4
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:19,014
Step one is the constructor. It's just a regular function, with

5
00:00:19,114 --> 00:00:22,949
a capital letter by convention. The exam usually asks for default

6
00:00:23,049 --> 00:00:25,856
values, so put them right in the parameter list.

7
00:00:25,933 --> 00:00:29,239
When you call it with new, JavaScript creates a brand-new

8
00:00:29,339 --> 00:00:32,167
empty object and makes this point to it. So these

9
00:00:32,267 --> 00:00:34,737
two lines store the data on the new object.

10
00:00:34,833 --> 00:00:38,062
Only data goes in the constructor. Methods go somewhere

11
00:00:38,162 --> 00:00:40,301
else, and you'll see why in a second.

12
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:44,794
i1 passed nothing, so both defaults kick in. i2 passed only the

13
00:00:44,894 --> 00:00:49,456
policy number, so the expiration date still falls back to its default.

14
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:56,465
Step two: methods go on the prototype. Why? Every object made by

15
00:00:56,565 --> 00:01:01,002
Insurance shares the same prototype, so there's exactly one copy of each

16
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:05,161
method. If you wrote this dot getInfo equals a function inside the

17
00:01:05,261 --> 00:01:09,697
constructor, every single object would get its own copy, and that wastes

18
00:01:09,797 --> 00:01:12,785
memory. The exam likes to ask about exactly that.

19
00:01:12,866 --> 00:01:15,905
There are two ways to do it. Option A replaces the

20
00:01:16,005 --> 00:01:20,110
entire prototype with an object literal that holds all the methods.

21
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:24,469
Look at this line. Because we threw away the original prototype object, we

22
00:01:24,569 --> 00:01:28,308
lost its constructor property, so we have to put it back by hand.

23
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:30,926
Option B adds one method at a time to the

24
00:01:31,026 --> 00:01:35,476
existing prototype. Nothing gets replaced, so constructor stays intact.

25
00:01:35,866 --> 00:01:39,200
Either way, any Insurance object can call getInfo, and

26
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,934
this refers to the object it was called on.

27
00:01:43,033 --> 00:01:45,697
Exam trap. If you replace the prototype with

28
00:01:45,797 --> 00:01:48,901
an object literal, the constructor property is gone

29
00:01:49,001 --> 00:01:52,293
unless you write constructor colon Insurance yourself.

30
00:01:55,366 --> 00:02:00,024
Let's prove both claims. Here A's prototype is replaced without a constructor

31
00:02:00,124 --> 00:02:03,916
property. So when we ask x for its constructor, the lookup goes

32
00:02:04,016 --> 00:02:07,314
past A's prototype all the way to Object dot prototype.

33
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:10,520
And here, Slow defines get inside the constructor,

34
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:13,225
so two Slow objects have two different get

35
00:02:13,325 --> 00:02:16,252
functions. Insurance objects share one getInfo.

36
00:02:16,633 --> 00:02:19,182
So x dot constructor is Object, not A. The

37
00:02:19,282 --> 00:02:22,526
two Slow methods are different functions, and the two

38
00:02:22,626 --> 00:02:25,365
Insurance methods are the very same function.

39
00:02:28,433 --> 00:02:31,866
Step three, inheritance. The child constructor takes

40
00:02:31,966 --> 00:02:34,381
the parent's parameters plus its own.

41
00:02:34,466 --> 00:02:38,348
Insurance dot call, with this as the first argument, runs the

42
00:02:38,448 --> 00:02:42,917
parent constructor on the new child object. That sets policyNumber and

43
00:02:43,017 --> 00:02:46,702
exp. This is the default-pattern version of calling super.

44
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,788
Then the child sets its own field.

45
00:02:48,866 --> 00:02:52,340
Next, link the prototypes. Object dot create makes a new

46
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:56,233
empty object whose proto is Insurance dot prototype, so every

47
00:02:56,333 --> 00:02:59,999
car insurance object can find getInfo. Some answer keys use

48
00:03:00,099 --> 00:03:02,998
new Insurance here instead, and that works too.

49
00:03:03,066 --> 00:03:07,070
And finally, repair the constructor so it points at CarInsurance.

50
00:03:07,466 --> 00:03:09,561
Exam trap. If you forget to reset the

51
00:03:09,661 --> 00:03:13,833
constructor, CarInsurance objects report Insurance as their constructor,

52
00:03:13,933 --> 00:03:16,918
because they inherit it from the parent's prototype.

53
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,928
Here are those three lines one more time, because you'll write them

54
00:03:24,028 --> 00:03:28,078
on every exam. Call copies the parent's fields onto the child. Object

55
00:03:28,178 --> 00:03:32,648
dot create links the prototypes so the child inherits methods. And resetting

56
00:03:32,748 --> 00:03:36,076
constructor fixes the one thing Object dot create breaks.

57
00:03:38,166 --> 00:03:42,731
Step four, overriding. Put a getInfo on the child's prototype. Lookup

58
00:03:42,831 --> 00:03:46,178
finds this one first, so it wins over the parent's.

59
00:03:46,266 --> 00:03:49,578
To reuse the parent's version, grab it from Insurance dot

60
00:03:49,678 --> 00:03:53,588
prototype and call it with this. That's the default-pattern version

61
00:03:53,688 --> 00:03:56,222
of super dot getInfo. Then append the plate.

62
00:03:56,300 --> 00:04:00,329
One ordering rule: add child methods after the Object dot create

63
00:04:00,429 --> 00:04:05,104
line. Otherwise, the assignment replaces the prototype and wipes them out.

64
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:07,069
Now let's test it, including a car

65
00:04:07,169 --> 00:04:09,444
insurance made with only a policy number.

66
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:12,775
The override works, instanceof is true for both the

67
00:04:12,875 --> 00:04:15,937
child and the parent, the constructor is correct, and

68
00:04:16,037 --> 00:04:19,098
the missing expiration date fell back to the parent's

69
00:04:19,198 --> 00:04:22,141
default, because undefined was passed through call.

70
00:04:25,233 --> 00:04:30,100
Practice question 1. Using the Default Pattern, with no class keyword, define

71
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:33,519
Pet with a name and an age, both with defaults, and a

72
00:04:33,619 --> 00:04:38,035
describe method on the prototype. Then define Dog, which adds a breed,

73
00:04:38,135 --> 00:04:42,679
inherits from Pet, and overrides describe to add the breed while reusing

74
00:04:42,779 --> 00:04:45,389
Pet's version. Pause the video and try it.

75
00:04:53,666 --> 00:04:57,475
The Pet constructor stores the data, and describe goes on the

76
00:04:57,575 --> 00:05:00,936
prototype. For Dog, call Pet with this to set name and

77
00:05:01,036 --> 00:05:05,037
age, then set breed. Link the prototypes with Object dot create,

78
00:05:05,137 --> 00:05:09,394
restore the constructor, and only then add the override, which calls

79
00:05:09,494 --> 00:05:12,406
Pet's describe with this and appends the breed.

80
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:20,720
Practice question 2. What does this print? Pause the video and try it.

81
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:32,815
It prints playing Fight, then false. play works fine because it's

82
00:05:32,915 --> 00:05:37,032
on the prototype. But the prototype was replaced without a constructor

83
00:05:37,132 --> 00:05:40,707
property, so s dot constructor is found further up the chain,

84
00:05:40,807 --> 00:05:43,780
on Object dot prototype, and it's Object, not Song.

85
00:05:47,866 --> 00:05:52,050
Recap. Data goes in the constructor, with default parameters. Methods

86
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:55,278
go on the prototype, so there's one shared copy. For

87
00:05:55,378 --> 00:05:58,692
a child, call the parent with this, link the prototypes

88
00:05:58,792 --> 00:06:02,665
with Object dot create, restore the constructor, and override by

89
00:06:02,765 --> 00:06:05,334
calling the parent's method with call this.

